countdowns.body:
Three changes for DC, Maryland and Virginia employers:

- Social Security wage base: {base26:usd0} to {base27:usd0}
- Maryland FAMLI: {famli:pct2} of wages; employers with {thr:int}+ employees pay at least {er:pct2}
- Virginia minimum wage: {vaCur:usd2} to {vaNew:usd2}

Unemployment-insurance rates and county wage floors are on the index.

releases.body:
What does one employee cost an employer in statutory taxes in DC, Maryland and Virginia? We built the answer from primary sources.

- New-employer unemployment insurance: DC {dc:pct2} on {dcBase:usd0}, MD {md:pct2} on {mdBase:usd0}, VA {va:pct2} on {vaBase:usd0}
- DC Paid Family Leave: {pfl:pct2} of wages, employer-paid
- Maryland FAMLI: {famli:pct2} from {famliStart:year}

Every figure links to its source. Free, no sign-up.
